# The build needs the two packages, the frontend, the ui-kit, the campaigns and
# docker/dependencies.txt. Everything else only slows the context transfer
# down, and some of it would poison the image: a .venv built for another path,
# or a node_modules built for another platform.
#
# This stays at the repository root while the Dockerfile lives in docker/,
# because Docker reads the ignore list from the root of the build context and
# the context is the repository.

# The desktop app is the other way of shipping this, and none of it belongs in
# the image. Left in, its CPython runtime and the installers in dist/ put the
# best part of a gigabyte through the context on every build.
app/
dist/

.ci-cache/
.devcontainer/
.git/
.github/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/

**/__pycache__/
**/*.egg-info/
**/*.py[cod]
**/node_modules/

build/
docs/
files/
frontend/dist/
output/
tmp/
web_dist/
